<figure id="alg1" class="ltx_float ltx_algorithm ltx_framed ltx_framed_top">
<figcaption class="ltx_caption"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_float"><span id="alg1.4" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Algorithm 1</span> </span><span id="alg1.5" class="ltx_text ltx_font_smallcaps">MVSS with Joint Diffusion</span>
</figcaption>
<div id="alg1.6" class="ltx_listing ltx_lst_numbers_left ltx_framed ltx_framed_topbottom ltx_listing">
<div id="alg1.6.1" class="ltx_listingline"><span id="alg1.6.1.1" class="ltx_text"><span id="alg1.6.1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Input:</span> </span>Dataset <math id="alg1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathcal{D}=\bigl\{\!\mathbf{y}^{\alpha}_{i_{\alpha}},\{\mathbf{A}^{\alpha\beta}_{i_{\alpha}}\}_{\beta=1}^{N_{s}},\mathbf{\Sigma}^{\alpha}_{i_{\alpha}}\bigr\}_{\alpha=1}^{N_{\text{views}}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒟</mi><mo>=</mo><msubsup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">{</mo><msubsup><mi>𝐲</mi><msub><mi>i</mi><mi>α</mi></msub><mi>α</mi></msubsup><mo>,</mo><msubsup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">{</mo><msubsup><mi>𝐀</mi><msub><mi>i</mi><mi>α</mi></msub><mrow><mi>α</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>β</mi></mrow></msubsup><mo stretchy="false">}</mo></mrow><mrow><mi>β</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><msub><mi>N</mi><mi>s</mi></msub></msubsup><mo>,</mo><msubsup><mi>𝚺</mi><msub><mi>i</mi><mi>α</mi></msub><mi>α</mi></msubsup><mo stretchy="false">}</mo></mrow><mrow><mi>α</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><msub><mi>N</mi><mtext>views</mtext></msub></msubsup></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathcal{D}=\bigl\{\!\mathbf{y}^{\alpha}_{i_{\alpha}},\{\mathbf{A}^{\alpha\beta}_{i_{\alpha}}\}_{\beta=1}^{N_{s}},\mathbf{\Sigma}^{\alpha}_{i_{\alpha}}\bigr\}_{\alpha=1}^{N_{\text{views}}}</annotation></semantics></math>,
number of sources <math id="alg1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="N_{s}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>N</mi><mi>s</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">N_{s}</annotation></semantics></math>, number of views <math id="alg1.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="N_{\text{views}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>N</mi><mtext>views</mtext></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">N_{\text{views}}</annotation></semantics></math>,
initial denoiser parameters
<math id="alg1.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\Theta_{0}=\{\theta^{\beta}_{0}\}_{\beta=1}^{N_{s}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi mathvariant="normal">Θ</mi><mn>0</mn></msub><mo>=</mo><msubsup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">{</mo><msubsup><mi>θ</mi><mn>0</mn><mi>β</mi></msubsup><mo stretchy="false">}</mo></mrow><mrow><mi>β</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><msub><mi>N</mi><mi>s</mi></msub></msubsup></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\Theta_{0}=\{\theta^{\beta}_{0}\}_{\beta=1}^{N_{s}}</annotation></semantics></math>,
number of EM rounds <math id="alg1.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="K" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>K</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">K</annotation></semantics></math>

</div>
<div id="alg1.6.2" class="ltx_listingline"><span id="alg1.6.2.1" class="ltx_text"><span id="alg1.6.2.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Output:</span> </span>Trained diffusion model priors with denoiser parameters <math id="alg1.m6" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\Theta_{K}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi mathvariant="normal">Θ</mi><mi>K</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\Theta_{K}</annotation></semantics></math>
</div>
<div id="alg1.6.3" class="ltx_listingline"><span id="alg1.6.3.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">for</span> <em id="alg1.6.3.2" class="ltx_emph ltx_font_italic"><math id="alg1.m7" class="ltx_Math" alttext="k\leftarrow 0" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>k</mi><mo stretchy="false">←</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">k\leftarrow 0</annotation></semantics></math> <span id="alg1.6.3.2.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">to</span> <math id="alg1.m8" class="ltx_Math" alttext="K-1" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>K</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">K-1</annotation></semantics></math></em> <span id="alg1.6.3.3" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">do</span>
</div>
<div id="alg1.6.4" class="ltx_listingline"> <span class="ltx_rule" style="width:1px;height:100%;--ltx-bg-color:black;display:inline-block;"> </span> <span id="alg1.6.4.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">foreach</span> <em id="alg1.6.4.2" class="ltx_emph ltx_font_italic">
<math id="alg1.m9" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\bigl(\mathbf{y}^{\alpha}_{i_{\alpha}},\{\mathbf{A}^{\alpha\beta}_{i_{\alpha}}\},\mathbf{\Sigma}^{\alpha}_{i_{\alpha}}\bigr)\in\mathcal{D}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mo maxsize="1.200em" minsize="1.200em">(</mo><msubsup><mi>𝐲</mi><msub><mi>i</mi><mi>α</mi></msub><mi>α</mi></msubsup><mo>,</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">{</mo><msubsup><mi>𝐀</mi><msub><mi>i</mi><mi>α</mi></msub><mrow><mi>α</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>β</mi></mrow></msubsup><mo stretchy="false">}</mo></mrow><mo>,</mo><msubsup><mi>𝚺</mi><msub><mi>i</mi><mi>α</mi></msub><mi>α</mi></msubsup><mo maxsize="1.200em" minsize="1.200em">)</mo></mrow><mo>∈</mo><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒟</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\bigl(\mathbf{y}^{\alpha}_{i_{\alpha}},\{\mathbf{A}^{\alpha\beta}_{i_{\alpha}}\},\mathbf{\Sigma}^{\alpha}_{i_{\alpha}}\bigr)\in\mathcal{D}</annotation></semantics></math></em> <span id="alg1.6.4.3" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">do</span>
</div>
<div id="alg1.6.5" class="ltx_listingline"> <span class="ltx_rule" style="width:1px;height:100%;--ltx-bg-color:black;display:inline-block;"> </span>  <span class="ltx_rule" style="width:1px;height:100%;--ltx-bg-color:black;display:inline-block;"> </span> <math id="alg1.m10" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\bigl\{\mathbf{x}^{\beta}_{i_{\alpha}}\bigr\}_{\beta=1}^{N_{s}}\sim q_{\Theta_{k}}\!\left(\{\mathbf{x}^{\beta}\}|\mathbf{y}^{\alpha}_{i_{\alpha}},\{\mathbf{A}^{\alpha\beta}_{i_{\alpha}}\}\right)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msubsup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">{</mo><msubsup><mi>𝐱</mi><msub><mi>i</mi><mi>α</mi></msub><mi>β</mi></msubsup><mo stretchy="false">}</mo></mrow><mrow><mi>β</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><msub><mi>N</mi><mi>s</mi></msub></msubsup><mo>∼</mo><mrow><msub><mi>q</mi><msub><mi mathvariant="normal">Θ</mi><mi>k</mi></msub></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo>(</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">{</mo><msup><mi>𝐱</mi><mi>β</mi></msup><mo stretchy="false">}</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">|</mo><mrow><msubsup><mi>𝐲</mi><msub><mi>i</mi><mi>α</mi></msub><mi>α</mi></msubsup><mo>,</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">{</mo><msubsup><mi>𝐀</mi><msub><mi>i</mi><mi>α</mi></msub><mrow><mi>α</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>β</mi></mrow></msubsup><mo stretchy="false">}</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\bigl\{\mathbf{x}^{\beta}_{i_{\alpha}}\bigr\}_{\beta=1}^{N_{s}}\sim q_{\Theta_{k}}\!\left(\{\mathbf{x}^{\beta}\}|\mathbf{y}^{\alpha}_{i_{\alpha}},\{\mathbf{A}^{\alpha\beta}_{i_{\alpha}}\}\right)</annotation></semantics></math> <span id="alg1.6.5.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_typewriter">// </span><span id="alg1.6.5.2" class="ltx_text ltx_font_typewriter">E step using equation <a href="#S4.E14" title="In 4 Methods ‣ A Data-Driven Prism: Multi-View Source Separation with Diffusion Model Priors" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">14</span></a> </span>
</div>
<div id="alg1.6.6" class="ltx_listingline"> <span class="ltx_rule" style="width:1px;height:100%;--ltx-bg-color:black;display:inline-block;"> </span> end foreach
</div>
<div id="alg1.6.7" class="ltx_listingline"> <span class="ltx_rule" style="width:1px;height:100%;--ltx-bg-color:black;display:inline-block;"> </span> <math id="alg1.m11" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\Theta_{k+1}=\argmax_{\Theta}\bigl[\sum_{i_{\alpha}}\sum_{\beta}\log q_{\theta^{\beta}}(\mathbf{x}^{\beta}_{i_{\alpha}})\bigr]" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi mathvariant="normal">Θ</mi><mrow><mi>k</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msub><mo>=</mo><mrow><msub><mrow><mi>arg</mi><mo lspace="0.170em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>max</mi></mrow><mi mathvariant="normal">Θ</mi></msub><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo maxsize="1.200em" minsize="1.200em">[</mo><mrow><msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">∑</mo><msub><mi>i</mi><mi>α</mi></msub></msub><mrow><msub><mo>∑</mo><mi>β</mi></msub><mrow><mrow><mi>log</mi><mo lspace="0.167em">⁡</mo><msub><mi>q</mi><msup><mi>θ</mi><mi>β</mi></msup></msub></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msubsup><mi>𝐱</mi><msub><mi>i</mi><mi>α</mi></msub><mi>β</mi></msubsup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo maxsize="1.200em" minsize="1.200em">]</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\Theta_{k+1}=\argmax_{\Theta}\bigl[\sum_{i_{\alpha}}\sum_{\beta}\log q_{\theta^{\beta}}(\mathbf{x}^{\beta}_{i_{\alpha}})\bigr]</annotation></semantics></math> <span id="alg1.6.7.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_typewriter">// </span><span id="alg1.6.7.2" class="ltx_text ltx_font_typewriter">M step using equation <a href="#S3.E5" title="In 3 Related Works ‣ A Data-Driven Prism: Multi-View Source Separation with Diffusion Model Priors" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">5</span></a> </span>
</div>
<div id="alg1.6.8" class="ltx_listingline">end for
</div>
<div id="alg1.6.9" class="ltx_listingline"><span id="alg1.6.9.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">return</span> <em id="alg1.6.9.2" class="ltx_emph ltx_font_italic"><math id="alg1.m12" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\Theta_{K}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi mathvariant="normal">Θ</mi><mi>K</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\Theta_{K}</annotation></semantics></math></em>

</div>
</div>
</figure>
<figure id="alg2" class="ltx_float ltx_algorithm ltx_framed ltx_framed_top">
<figcaption class="ltx_caption"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_float"><span id="alg2.4" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Algorithm 2</span> </span><span id="alg2.5" class="ltx_text ltx_font_smallcaps">Simplified Contrastive MVSS with Joint Diffusion</span>
</figcaption>
<div id="alg2.6" class="ltx_listing ltx_lst_numbers_left ltx_framed ltx_framed_topbottom ltx_listing">
<div id="alg2.6.1" class="ltx_listingline"><span id="alg2.6.1.1" class="ltx_text"><span id="alg2.6.1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Input:</span> </span>Dataset <math id="alg2.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathcal{D}=\bigl\{\!\mathbf{y}^{\alpha}_{i_{\alpha}},\{\mathbf{A}^{\alpha\beta}_{i_{\alpha}}\}_{\beta=1}^{N_{s}},\mathbf{\Sigma}^{\alpha}_{i_{\alpha}}\bigr\}_{\alpha=1}^{N_{\text{views}}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒟</mi><mo>=</mo><msubsup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">{</mo><msubsup><mi>𝐲</mi><msub><mi>i</mi><mi>α</mi></msub><mi>α</mi></msubsup><mo>,</mo><msubsup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">{</mo><msubsup><mi>𝐀</mi><msub><mi>i</mi><mi>α</mi></msub><mrow><mi>α</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>β</mi></mrow></msubsup><mo stretchy="false">}</mo></mrow><mrow><mi>β</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><msub><mi>N</mi><mi>s</mi></msub></msubsup><mo>,</mo><msubsup><mi>𝚺</mi><msub><mi>i</mi><mi>α</mi></msub><mi>α</mi></msubsup><mo stretchy="false">}</mo></mrow><mrow><mi>α</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><msub><mi>N</mi><mtext>views</mtext></msub></msubsup></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathcal{D}=\bigl\{\!\mathbf{y}^{\alpha}_{i_{\alpha}},\{\mathbf{A}^{\alpha\beta}_{i_{\alpha}}\}_{\beta=1}^{N_{s}},\mathbf{\Sigma}^{\alpha}_{i_{\alpha}}\bigr\}_{\alpha=1}^{N_{\text{views}}}</annotation></semantics></math>,
<math id="alg2.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathbf{A}^{\alpha\beta}_{i_{\alpha}}=0" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msubsup><mi>𝐀</mi><msub><mi>i</mi><mi>α</mi></msub><mrow><mi>α</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>β</mi></mrow></msubsup><mo>=</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathbf{A}^{\alpha\beta}_{i_{\alpha}}=0</annotation></semantics></math> if <math id="alg2.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\beta&gt;\alpha" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>β</mi><mo>&gt;</mo><mi>α</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\beta&gt;\alpha</annotation></semantics></math>,
number of sources <math id="alg2.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="N_{s}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>N</mi><mi>s</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">N_{s}</annotation></semantics></math>, number of views <math id="alg2.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="N_{\text{views}}=N_{s}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>N</mi><mtext>views</mtext></msub><mo>=</mo><msub><mi>N</mi><mi>s</mi></msub></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">N_{\text{views}}=N_{s}</annotation></semantics></math>,
initial denoiser parameters
<math id="alg2.m6" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\Theta_{0}=\{\theta^{\beta}_{0}\}_{\beta=1}^{N_{s}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi mathvariant="normal">Θ</mi><mn>0</mn></msub><mo>=</mo><msubsup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">{</mo><msubsup><mi>θ</mi><mn>0</mn><mi>β</mi></msubsup><mo stretchy="false">}</mo></mrow><mrow><mi>β</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><msub><mi>N</mi><mi>s</mi></msub></msubsup></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\Theta_{0}=\{\theta^{\beta}_{0}\}_{\beta=1}^{N_{s}}</annotation></semantics></math>,
number of EM rounds <math id="alg2.m7" class="ltx_Math" alttext="K" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>K</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">K</annotation></semantics></math>

</div>
<div id="alg2.6.2" class="ltx_listingline"><span id="alg2.6.2.1" class="ltx_text"><span id="alg2.6.2.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Output:</span> </span>Trained diffusion model priors with denoiser parameters <math id="alg2.m8" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\Theta_{K}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi mathvariant="normal">Θ</mi><mi>K</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\Theta_{K}</annotation></semantics></math>
</div>
<div id="alg2.6.3" class="ltx_listingline"><span id="alg2.6.3.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">for</span> <em id="alg2.6.3.2" class="ltx_emph ltx_font_italic"><math id="alg2.m9" class="ltx_Math" alttext="a\leftarrow 1" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>a</mi><mo stretchy="false">←</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">a\leftarrow 1</annotation></semantics></math> <span id="alg2.6.3.2.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">to</span> <math id="alg2.m10" class="ltx_Math" alttext="N_{\text{views}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>N</mi><mtext class="ltx_mathvariant_italic">views</mtext></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">N_{\text{views}}</annotation></semantics></math></em> <span id="alg2.6.3.3" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">do</span>
</div>
<div id="alg2.6.4" class="ltx_listingline"> <span class="ltx_rule" style="width:1px;height:100%;--ltx-bg-color:black;display:inline-block;"> </span> <span id="alg2.6.4.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">for</span> <em id="alg2.6.4.2" class="ltx_emph ltx_font_italic"><math id="alg2.m11" class="ltx_Math" alttext="k\leftarrow 0" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>k</mi><mo stretchy="false">←</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">k\leftarrow 0</annotation></semantics></math> <span id="alg2.6.4.2.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">to</span> <math id="alg2.m12" class="ltx_Math" alttext="K-1" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>K</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">K-1</annotation></semantics></math></em> <span id="alg2.6.4.3" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">do</span>
</div>
<div id="alg2.6.5" class="ltx_listingline"> <span class="ltx_rule" style="width:1px;height:100%;--ltx-bg-color:black;display:inline-block;"> </span>  <span class="ltx_rule" style="width:1px;height:100%;--ltx-bg-color:black;display:inline-block;"> </span> <span id="alg2.6.5.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">foreach</span> <em id="alg2.6.5.2" class="ltx_emph ltx_font_italic">
<math id="alg2.m13" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\bigl(\mathbf{y}^{\alpha}_{i_{\alpha}},\{\mathbf{A}^{\alpha\beta}_{i_{\alpha}}\},\mathbf{\Sigma}^{\alpha}_{i_{\alpha}}\bigr)\in\mathcal{D}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mo maxsize="1.200em" minsize="1.200em">(</mo><msubsup><mi>𝐲</mi><msub><mi>i</mi><mi>α</mi></msub><mi>α</mi></msubsup><mo>,</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">{</mo><msubsup><mi>𝐀</mi><msub><mi>i</mi><mi>α</mi></msub><mrow><mi>α</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>β</mi></mrow></msubsup><mo stretchy="false">}</mo></mrow><mo>,</mo><msubsup><mi>𝚺</mi><msub><mi>i</mi><mi>α</mi></msub><mi>α</mi></msubsup><mo maxsize="1.200em" minsize="1.200em">)</mo></mrow><mo>∈</mo><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒟</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\bigl(\mathbf{y}^{\alpha}_{i_{\alpha}},\{\mathbf{A}^{\alpha\beta}_{i_{\alpha}}\},\mathbf{\Sigma}^{\alpha}_{i_{\alpha}}\bigr)\in\mathcal{D}</annotation></semantics></math> with <math id="alg2.m14" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\alpha=a" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>α</mi><mo>=</mo><mi>a</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\alpha=a</annotation></semantics></math></em> <span id="alg2.6.5.3" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">do</span>
</div>
<div id="alg2.6.6" class="ltx_listingline"> <span class="ltx_rule" style="width:1px;height:100%;--ltx-bg-color:black;display:inline-block;"> </span>  <span class="ltx_rule" style="width:1px;height:100%;--ltx-bg-color:black;display:inline-block;"> </span>  <span class="ltx_rule" style="width:1px;height:100%;--ltx-bg-color:black;display:inline-block;"> </span> <math id="alg2.m15" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\bigl\{\mathbf{x}^{\beta}_{i_{\alpha}}\bigr\}_{\beta=1}^{a}\sim q_{\{\theta_{k}^{\beta}\}_{\beta=1}^{a}}\!\left(\{\mathbf{x}^{\beta}\}|\mathbf{y}^{\alpha}_{i_{\alpha}},\{\mathbf{A}^{\alpha\beta}_{i_{\alpha}}\}\right)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msubsup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">{</mo><msubsup><mi>𝐱</mi><msub><mi>i</mi><mi>α</mi></msub><mi>β</mi></msubsup><mo stretchy="false">}</mo></mrow><mrow><mi>β</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mi>a</mi></msubsup><mo>∼</mo><mrow><msub><mi>q</mi><msubsup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">{</mo><msubsup><mi>θ</mi><mi>k</mi><mi>β</mi></msubsup><mo stretchy="false">}</mo></mrow><mrow><mi>β</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mi>a</mi></msubsup></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo>(</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">{</mo><msup><mi>𝐱</mi><mi>β</mi></msup><mo stretchy="false">}</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">|</mo><mrow><msubsup><mi>𝐲</mi><msub><mi>i</mi><mi>α</mi></msub><mi>α</mi></msubsup><mo>,</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">{</mo><msubsup><mi>𝐀</mi><msub><mi>i</mi><mi>α</mi></msub><mrow><mi>α</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>β</mi></mrow></msubsup><mo stretchy="false">}</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\bigl\{\mathbf{x}^{\beta}_{i_{\alpha}}\bigr\}_{\beta=1}^{a}\sim q_{\{\theta_{k}^{\beta}\}_{\beta=1}^{a}}\!\left(\{\mathbf{x}^{\beta}\}|\mathbf{y}^{\alpha}_{i_{\alpha}},\{\mathbf{A}^{\alpha\beta}_{i_{\alpha}}\}\right)</annotation></semantics></math> <span id="alg2.6.6.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_typewriter">// </span><span id="alg2.6.6.2" class="ltx_text ltx_font_typewriter">E step using equation <a href="#S4.E14" title="In 4 Methods ‣ A Data-Driven Prism: Multi-View Source Separation with Diffusion Model Priors" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">14</span></a> </span>
</div>
<div id="alg2.6.7" class="ltx_listingline"> <span class="ltx_rule" style="width:1px;height:100%;--ltx-bg-color:black;display:inline-block;"> </span>  <span class="ltx_rule" style="width:1px;height:100%;--ltx-bg-color:black;display:inline-block;"> </span> end foreach
</div>
<div id="alg2.6.8" class="ltx_listingline"> <span class="ltx_rule" style="width:1px;height:100%;--ltx-bg-color:black;display:inline-block;"> </span>  <span class="ltx_rule" style="width:1px;height:100%;--ltx-bg-color:black;display:inline-block;"> </span> <math id="alg2.m16" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\theta_{k+1}^{a}=\argmax_{\theta^{a}}\bigl[\sum_{i_{\alpha}}\log q_{\theta^{a}}(\mathbf{x}^{a}_{i_{\alpha}})\bigr]" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msubsup><mi>θ</mi><mrow><mi>k</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mi>a</mi></msubsup><mo>=</mo><mrow><msub><mrow><mi>arg</mi><mo lspace="0.170em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>max</mi></mrow><msup><mi>θ</mi><mi>a</mi></msup></msub><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo maxsize="1.200em" minsize="1.200em">[</mo><mrow><msub><mo lspace="0em">∑</mo><msub><mi>i</mi><mi>α</mi></msub></msub><mrow><mrow><mi>log</mi><mo lspace="0.167em">⁡</mo><msub><mi>q</mi><msup><mi>θ</mi><mi>a</mi></msup></msub></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msubsup><mi>𝐱</mi><msub><mi>i</mi><mi>α</mi></msub><mi>a</mi></msubsup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo maxsize="1.200em" minsize="1.200em">]</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\theta_{k+1}^{a}=\argmax_{\theta^{a}}\bigl[\sum_{i_{\alpha}}\log q_{\theta^{a}}(\mathbf{x}^{a}_{i_{\alpha}})\bigr]</annotation></semantics></math> <span id="alg2.6.8.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_typewriter">// </span><span id="alg2.6.8.2" class="ltx_text ltx_font_typewriter">M step for only source <math id="alg2.m17" class="ltx_Math" alttext="a" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>a</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">a</annotation></semantics></math> </span>
</div>
<div id="alg2.6.9" class="ltx_listingline"> <span class="ltx_rule" style="width:1px;height:100%;--ltx-bg-color:black;display:inline-block;"> </span> end for
</div>
<div id="alg2.6.10" class="ltx_listingline">end for
</div>
<div id="alg2.6.11" class="ltx_listingline"><span id="alg2.6.11.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">return</span> <em id="alg2.6.11.2" class="ltx_emph ltx_font_italic"><math id="alg2.m18" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\Theta_{K}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi mathvariant="normal">Θ</mi><mi>K</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\Theta_{K}</annotation></semantics></math></em>

</div>
</div>
</figure>
<section id="A1" class="ltx_appendix">
<h2 class="ltx_title ltx_title_appendix"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_appendix">Appendix A </span>Joint Sampling Algorithms</h2>

<div id="A1.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A1.p1.1" class="ltx_p">In Algorithm <a href="#alg1" title="In A Data-Driven Prism: Multi-View Source Separation with Diffusion Model Priors" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">1</span></a> we present an algorithmic summary of our MVSS method using joint sampling. This method conducts a joint EM training for all sources simultaneously. In Algorithm <a href="#alg2" title="In A Data-Driven Prism: Multi-View Source Separation with Diffusion Model Priors" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">2</span></a> we present a summary of the contrastive MVSS simplification. This method trains each source sequentially under the assumption that view <math id="A1.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\alpha=1" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>α</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\alpha=1</annotation></semantics></math> only contains source <math id="A1.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\beta=1" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>β</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\beta=1</annotation></semantics></math>, view <math id="A1.p1.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\alpha=2" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>α</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>2</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\alpha=2</annotation></semantics></math> only contains sources <math id="A1.p1.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\beta\in\{1,2\}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>β</mi><mo>∈</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">{</mo><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>,</mo><mn>2</mn></mrow><mo stretchy="false">}</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\beta\in\{1,2\}</annotation></semantics></math>, and so on (see Section <a href="#S4" title="4 Methods ‣ A Data-Driven Prism: Multi-View Source Separation with Diffusion Model Priors" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">4</span></a>). While Algorithm <a href="#alg2" title="In A Data-Driven Prism: Multi-View Source Separation with Diffusion Model Priors" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">2</span></a> discards the information about source <math id="A1.p1.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\beta" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>β</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\beta</annotation></semantics></math> for views <math id="A1.p1.m6" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\alpha\neq\beta" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>α</mi><mo>≠</mo><mi>β</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\alpha\neq\beta</annotation></semantics></math>, it reduces the computational complexity.</p>
</div>
</section>
<section id="A2" class="ltx_appendix">
<h2 class="ltx_title ltx_title_appendix"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_appendix">Appendix B </span>Gibbs Sampling</h2>

<div id="A2.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A2.p1.1" class="ltx_p">Gibbs sampling with diffusion models, originally proposed for blind denoising <cite class="ltx_cite ltx_citemacro_cite">[<a href="#bib.bibx54" title="" class="ltx_ref">54</a>]</cite>, can be easily extended to the full MVSS problem. We start by selecting a source <math id="A2.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\beta_{g}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>β</mi><mi>g</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\beta_{g}</annotation></semantics></math>. Given the <math id="A2.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="t=0" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">t=0</annotation></semantics></math> source realizations for <math id="A2.p1.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\{\mathbf{x}^{\beta^{\prime}}_{0}\}_{\beta^{\prime}\neq\beta_{g}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">{</mo><msubsup><mi>𝐱</mi><mn>0</mn><msup><mi>β</mi><mo>′</mo></msup></msubsup><mo stretchy="false">}</mo></mrow><mrow><msup><mi>β</mi><mo>′</mo></msup><mo>≠</mo><msub><mi>β</mi><mi>g</mi></msub></mrow></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\{\mathbf{x}^{\beta^{\prime}}_{0}\}_{\beta^{\prime}\neq\beta_{g}}</annotation></semantics></math>, an observation <math id="A2.p1.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathbf{y}^{\alpha}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msup><mi>𝐲</mi><mi>α</mi></msup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathbf{y}^{\alpha}</annotation></semantics></math>, a set of known mixing matrices <math id="A2.p1.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\{\mathbf{A}^{\alpha\beta}\}_{\beta=1}^{N_{s}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msubsup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">{</mo><msup><mi>𝐀</mi><mrow><mi>α</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>β</mi></mrow></msup><mo stretchy="false">}</mo></mrow><mrow><mi>β</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><msub><mi>N</mi><mi>s</mi></msub></msubsup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\{\mathbf{A}^{\alpha\beta}\}_{\beta=1}^{N_{s}}</annotation></semantics></math>, and the noise covariance <math id="A2.p1.m6" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathbf{\Sigma}^{\alpha}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msup><mi>𝚺</mi><mi>α</mi></msup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathbf{\Sigma}^{\alpha}</annotation></semantics></math>, then the posterior score for the remaining source becomes:</p>
<table id="A2.E18" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A2.E18.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\begin{split}\nabla_{\mathbf{x}_{t}^{\beta_{g}}}\log p(\mathbf{x}_{t}^{\beta_{g}}|\mathbf{y}^{\alpha},\{\mathbf{A}^{\alpha\beta}\}_{\beta=1}^{N_{s}},\{\mathbf{x}^{\beta^{\prime}}_{0}\}_{\beta^{\prime}\neq\beta_{g}})=&amp;\nabla_{\mathbf{x}_{t}^{\beta_{g}}}\log p(\mathbf{x}_{t}^{\beta_{g}})\quad+\\
&amp;\nabla_{\mathbf{x}_{t}^{\beta_{g}}}\log p(\mathbf{y}^{\alpha}|\mathbf{x}_{t}^{\beta_{g}},\{\mathbf{A}^{\alpha\beta}\}_{\beta=1}^{N_{s}},\{\mathbf{x}^{\beta^{\prime}}_{0}\}_{\beta^{\prime}\neq\beta_{g}}).\end{split}" display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mtable columnspacing="0pt" displaystyle="true" rowspacing="0pt"><mtr><mtd class="ltx_align_right" columnalign="right"><mrow><mrow><msub><mo>∇</mo><msubsup><mi>𝐱</mi><mi>t</mi><msub><mi>β</mi><mi>g</mi></msub></msubsup></msub><mo lspace="0.167em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>log</mi><mo lspace="0.167em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>p</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msubsup><mi>𝐱</mi><mi>t</mi><msub><mi>β</mi><mi>g</mi></msub></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">|</mo><mrow><msup><mi>𝐲</mi><mi>α</mi></msup><mo>,</mo><msubsup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">{</mo><msup><mi>𝐀</mi><mrow><mi>α</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>β</mi></mrow></msup><mo stretchy="false">}</mo></mrow><mrow><mi>β</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><msub><mi>N</mi><mi>s</mi></msub></msubsup><mo>,</mo><msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">{</mo><msubsup><mi>𝐱</mi><mn>0</mn><msup><mi>β</mi><mo>′</mo></msup></msubsup><mo stretchy="false">}</mo></mrow><mrow><msup><mi>β</mi><mo>′</mo></msup><mo>≠</mo><msub><mi>β</mi><mi>g</mi></msub></mrow></msub></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mphantom></mphantom></mrow></mtd><mtd class="ltx_align_left" columnalign="left"><mrow><mrow><msub><mo>∇</mo><msubsup><mi>𝐱</mi><mi>t</mi><msub><mi>β</mi><mi>g</mi></msub></msubsup></msub><mo lspace="0.167em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>log</mi><mo lspace="0.167em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>p</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msubsup><mi>𝐱</mi><mi>t</mi><msub><mi>β</mi><mi>g</mi></msub></msubsup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mspace style="width:2.222em;" width="2.222em"></mspace><mo>+</mo></mrow></mtd></mtr><mtr><mtd></mtd><mtd class="ltx_align_left" columnalign="left"><mrow><mrow><msub><mo>∇</mo><msubsup><mi>𝐱</mi><mi>t</mi><msub><mi>β</mi><mi>g</mi></msub></msubsup></msub><mo lspace="0.167em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>log</mi><mo lspace="0.167em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>p</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msup><mi>𝐲</mi><mi>α</mi></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">|</mo><mrow><msubsup><mi>𝐱</mi><mi>t</mi><msub><mi>β</mi><mi>g</mi></msub></msubsup><mo>,</mo><msubsup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">{</mo><msup><mi>𝐀</mi><mrow><mi>α</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>β</mi></mrow></msup><mo stretchy="false">}</mo></mrow><mrow><mi>β</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><msub><mi>N</mi><mi>s</mi></msub></msubsup><mo>,</mo><msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">{</mo><msubsup><mi>𝐱</mi><mn>0</mn><msup><mi>β</mi><mo>′</mo></msup></msubsup><mo stretchy="false">}</mo></mrow><mrow><msup><mi>β</mi><mo>′</mo></msup><mo>≠</mo><msub><mi>β</mi><mi>g</mi></msub></mrow></msub></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow></mtd></mtr></mtable><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\begin{split}\nabla_{\mathbf{x}_{t}^{\beta_{g}}}\log p(\mathbf{x}_{t}^{\beta_{g}}|\mathbf{y}^{\alpha},\{\mathbf{A}^{\alpha\beta}\}_{\beta=1}^{N_{s}},\{\mathbf{x}^{\beta^{\prime}}_{0}\}_{\beta^{\prime}\neq\beta_{g}})=&amp;\nabla_{\mathbf{x}_{t}^{\beta_{g}}}\log p(\mathbf{x}_{t}^{\beta_{g}})\quad+\\
&amp;\nabla_{\mathbf{x}_{t}^{\beta_{g}}}\log p(\mathbf{y}^{\alpha}|\mathbf{x}_{t}^{\beta_{g}},\{\mathbf{A}^{\alpha\beta}\}_{\beta=1}^{N_{s}},\{\mathbf{x}^{\beta^{\prime}}_{0}\}_{\beta^{\prime}\neq\beta_{g}}).\end{split}</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(18)</span></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A2.p1.2" class="ltx_p">For conciseness, we can introduce the observation residual <math id="A2.p1.m7" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathbf{r}^{\alpha}=\mathbf{y}^{\alpha}-\sum_{\beta^{\prime}\neq\beta_{g}}\mathbf{A}^{\alpha\beta^{\prime}}\mathbf{x}_{0}^{\beta^{\prime}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msup><mi>𝐫</mi><mi>α</mi></msup><mo>=</mo><mrow><msup><mi>𝐲</mi><mi>α</mi></msup><mo rspace="0.055em">−</mo><mrow><msub><mo>∑</mo><mrow><msup><mi>β</mi><mo>′</mo></msup><mo>≠</mo><msub><mi>β</mi><mi>g</mi></msub></mrow></msub><mrow><msup><mi>𝐀</mi><mrow><mi>α</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mi>β</mi><mo>′</mo></msup></mrow></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msubsup><mi>𝐱</mi><mn>0</mn><msup><mi>β</mi><mo>′</mo></msup></msubsup></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathbf{r}^{\alpha}=\mathbf{y}^{\alpha}-\sum_{\beta^{\prime}\neq\beta_{g}}\mathbf{A}^{\alpha\beta^{\prime}}\mathbf{x}_{0}^{\beta^{\prime}}</annotation></semantics></math>. We can then write the remaining likelihood term in Equation <a href="#A2.E18" title="In Appendix B Gibbs Sampling ‣ A Data-Driven Prism: Multi-View Source Separation with Diffusion Model Priors" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">18</span></a> as:</p>
<table id="A2.EGx15" class="ltx_equationgroup ltx_eqn_align ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody id="A2.E19"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A2.E19.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle p(\mathbf{y}^{\alpha}|\mathbf{x}_{t}^{\beta_{g}},\{\mathbf{A}^{\alpha\beta}\}_{\beta=1}^{N_{s}},\{\mathbf{x}^{\beta^{\prime}}\}_{\beta^{\prime}\neq\beta_{g}})=\int p(\mathbf{r}^{\alpha}|\mathbf{x}^{\beta_{g}}_{0})p(\mathbf{x}^{\beta_{g}}_{0}|\mathbf{x}^{\beta_{g}}_{t})\text{d}\mathbf{x}^{\beta_{g}}_{0}," display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><mi>p</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msup><mi>𝐲</mi><mi>α</mi></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">|</mo><mrow><msubsup><mi>𝐱</mi><mi>t</mi><msub><mi>β</mi><mi>g</mi></msub></msubsup><mo>,</mo><msubsup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">{</mo><msup><mi>𝐀</mi><mrow><mi>α</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>β</mi></mrow></msup><mo stretchy="false">}</mo></mrow><mrow><mi>β</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><msub><mi>N</mi><mi>s</mi></msub></msubsup><mo>,</mo><msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">{</mo><msup><mi>𝐱</mi><msup><mi>β</mi><mo>′</mo></msup></msup><mo stretchy="false">}</mo></mrow><mrow><msup><mi>β</mi><mo>′</mo></msup><mo>≠</mo><msub><mi>β</mi><mi>g</mi></msub></mrow></msub></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mrow><mo>∫</mo><mrow><mrow><mi>p</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msup><mi>𝐫</mi><mi>α</mi></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">|</mo><msubsup><mi>𝐱</mi><mn>0</mn><msub><mi>β</mi><mi>g</mi></msub></msubsup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>p</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msubsup><mi>𝐱</mi><mn>0</mn><msub><mi>β</mi><mi>g</mi></msub></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">|</mo><msubsup><mi>𝐱</mi><mi>t</mi><msub><mi>β</mi><mi>g</mi></msub></msubsup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mtext>d</mtext><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msubsup><mi>𝐱</mi><mn>0</mn><msub><mi>β</mi><mi>g</mi></msub></msubsup></mrow></mrow></mstyle></mrow><mo>,</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle p(\mathbf{y}^{\alpha}|\mathbf{x}_{t}^{\beta_{g}},\{\mathbf{A}^{\alpha\beta}\}_{\beta=1}^{N_{s}},\{\mathbf{x}^{\beta^{\prime}}\}_{\beta^{\prime}\neq\beta_{g}})=\int p(\mathbf{r}^{\alpha}|\mathbf{x}^{\beta_{g}}_{0})p(\mathbf{x}^{\beta_{g}}_{0}|\mathbf{x}^{\beta_{g}}_{t})\text{d}\mathbf{x}^{\beta_{g}}_{0},</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(19)</span></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A2.p1.3" class="ltx_p">which is identical to Equation <a href="#S3.E7" title="In 3 Related Works ‣ A Data-Driven Prism: Multi-View Source Separation with Diffusion Model Priors" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">7</span></a> with the observation replaced by the residual. Since Gibbs sampling fixes all but one source at a time, the posterior evaluation reduces to traditional posterior sampling with a diffusion prior with the observation replaced by the residual. An implementation of the Gibbs sampling procedure for MVSS can be found in the provided code.</p>
</div>
</section>
<section id="A3" class="ltx_appendix">
<h2 class="ltx_title ltx_title_appendix"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_appendix">Appendix C </span>One-Dimensional Manifold Experiment Details</h2>

<div id="A3.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A3.p1.1" class="ltx_p">We generate random one-dimensional manifolds following the steps outlined in <cite class="ltx_cite ltx_citemacro_cite">[<a href="#bib.bibx65" title="" class="ltx_ref">65</a>]</cite>. In all experiments in Section <a href="#S5.SS1" title="5.1 One-Dimensional Manifold Experiments ‣ 5 Results ‣ A Data-Driven Prism: Multi-View Source Separation with Diffusion Model Priors" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">5.1</span></a>, the smoothness parameters for the manifolds corresponding to the first, second, and third source distributions are set to <math id="A3.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="3,4," display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mn>3</mn><mo>,</mo><mn>4</mn></mrow><mo>,</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">3,4,</annotation></semantics></math> and <math id="A3.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="5" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mn>5</mn><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">5</annotation></semantics></math> respectively. Similarly, we use the same denoiser architecture for each source and each experiment. The denoiser is a multi-layer perceptron (MLP) composed of 3 hidden layers with 256 neurons and SiLU activation function <cite class="ltx_cite ltx_citemacro_cite">[<a href="#bib.bibx66" title="" class="ltx_ref">66</a>]</cite>, followed by a layer normalization function <cite class="ltx_cite ltx_citemacro_cite">[<a href="#bib.bibx67" title="" class="ltx_ref">67</a>]</cite>. The denoiser is conditioned on noise and noise embeddings are generated with the sinusoidal positional encoding method <cite class="ltx_cite ltx_citemacro_cite">[<a href="#bib.bibx60" title="" class="ltx_ref">60</a>]</cite>.</p>
</div>
<div id="A3.p2" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A3.p2.1" class="ltx_p">For the metrics, we use 16384 samples for the Sinkhorn divergence evaluation, 1024 samples for the PQMass evaluation, and 16384 samples for the PSNR evaluation. Note that we use the same number of samples from the true distribution and the prior / posterior distribution for all metrics. Metrics on the posterior samples are calculated by comparing to the true source value for the corresponding observation. For the PQMass evaluation, we use <math id="A3.p2.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="1000" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mn>1000</mn><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">1000</annotation></semantics></math> tessellations and otherwise keep the default parameters.</p>
</div>
<section id="A3.SS1" class="ltx_subsection">
<h3 class="ltx_title ltx_title_subsection"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_subsection">C.1 </span>Contrastive MVSS</h3>

<div id="A3.SS1.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A3.SS1.p1.1" class="ltx_p">In the contrastive MVSS experiment, we use the simplified contrastive MVSS algorithm to train the denoiser models. We train the <math id="A3.SS1.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\beta=1,2,3" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi>β</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mo>,</mo><mn>2</mn><mo>,</mo><mn>3</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\beta=1,2,3</annotation></semantics></math> denoiser models for 16, 32, and 64 EM laps respectively. Following <cite class="ltx_cite ltx_citemacro_cite">[<a href="#bib.bibx40" title="" class="ltx_ref">40</a>]</cite>, we reinitialize the optimizer and learning rate after each EM lap while keeping the current denoiser parameters. The MLP takes as input a concatenated vector of the diffused sample at time <math id="A3.SS1.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="t" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>t</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">t</annotation></semantics></math> and the corresponding noise embedding. We summarize other training hyperparameters in Table <a href="#A3.T2" title="Table 2 ‣ C.1 Contrastive MVSS ‣ Appendix C One-Dimensional Manifold Experiment Details ‣ A Data-Driven Prism: Multi-View Source Separation with Diffusion Model Priors" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">2</span></a>.</p>
</div>
